The man Zam is the brother of the husband of the daughter of the woman Jin,
which makes him Jin's son-in-law.

In the original translation, I have {jy. be'aspe la.zam.}, which is
obviously wrong.

So, let's see. {jy. mamta lo speni be lo bruna be la.zam.} is {jy.
be'aspemamta la.zam.}? Is there some way to make that shorter?

